<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomás Herrera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1854</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomás Herrera was a Panamanian soldier and politician who fought in the wars of independence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. In 1840 he became head of the short-lived State of the Isthmus, which seceded from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> until 1841. He later served as acting president of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in 1854 and was killed that year fighting against the dictatorship of José María Melo.</p></div>
